; code.ctt — codes of terms as data (Scott encoding), and the evaluator as a term.
; A code is a function of one handler per constructor; variables are de Bruijn
; indices (Church numerals) into an environment of nested pairs; a binder's body
; is a code under one more variable. eval maps a code and an environment to the
; value the machine gives the term. A question about the evaluator is a term.

(def cvar (lam n (lam h-var h-lam h-app h-pair h-fst h-snd h-pi h-sigma h-univ h-pathp h-plam h-papp h-pappe h-i0 h-i1 h-neg h-meet h-join h-eq0 h-eq1 h-fand h-for h-ftt h-fff h-forall h-faceof h-sys0 h-sysc h-sysmap h-comp h-gluet h-glue h-unglue h-let (h-var n))))
